Appendix G. Robust Feasibility

G.1 Set-inclusion monotonicity

Proposition G.1. If $\mathcal{W}_1 \subseteq \mathcal{W}_2$, then $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{W}_2) \subseteq \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{W}_1)$.

Proof. A control $u$ satisfying all constraints for all $w \in \mathcal{W}_2$ also satisfies them for all $w \in \mathcal{W}_1 \subseteq \mathcal{W}_2$. The converse is not true in general. $\square$

Corollary G.1. If $\mathcal{U}_{\theta, 1} \subseteq \mathcal{U}_{\theta, 2}$, then $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{U}_{\theta, 2}) \subseteq \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{U}_{\theta, 1})$.

G.2 Feasibility mapping: monotonicity theorem

Theorem G.1. For a fixed system, robust feasibility is:
(i) non-increasing in $\sigma_W$;
(ii) non-increasing in the size of $\mathcal{U}_\theta$;
(iii) non-decreasing in the available safety margin.

Proof. (i) and (ii) follow from Proposition G.1. (iii) A larger safety margin relaxes the effective constraint set, expanding the feasible region. $\square$

G.3 Vector margin formulation

Definition G.1. For constraints $g_j(x, u, w, \theta) \leq 0$, $j = 1, \dots, J$, robust feasibility is:

\exists u : \sup_{w \in \mathcal{W}_t, \theta \in \mathcal{U}_\theta, M \in \mathcal{U}_M} g_j(x, u, w, \theta, M) \leq 0, \quad \forall j \tag{G.1}

Critical correction (retained). The scalar bound $T_{d,i}^{\mathrm{nominal}} + \delta(\sigma_W) \leq T_{\max}$ covers only one thermal constraint. The vector formulation (G.1) is the correct general form, encompassing pressure, actuator, and rate constraints.

